(5472923, 786211, 36999, '<td valign="top">It''s Hoover Dam all right but it holds back Lake Mead, not Lake Powell.  Lake Powell is held back by Glen Canyon Dam a bit further upstream.  Killer perspective in this pic.  Love the wide angle and congrats on the top 10!</td>', 'It''s Hoover Dam all right but it holds back Lake Mead, not Lake Powell.  Lake Powell is held back by Glen Canyon Dam a bit further upstream.  Killer perspective in this pic.  Love the wide angle and congrats on the top 10!', '2009-05-06 15:17:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(5473109, 786036, 71657, '<td valign="top">Congrats Irene.   This is a wonderful picture.  No doubt if you would have used a green liquid, this would have definitely been a top 10.  However, this goes to show that you cannot do well in a challenge even if the picture is within challenge description.  The title of this picture is the only thing I see that has anything to do with green.  Other than that, this picture does not even meet the challenge description.  This picture should have been voted on by challenge description, not title.  This should have not done better than 50 percintile in this challenge, as it does not meet the challenge.  When are the voters going to vote on challenge descriptions and the thought that goes into them instead of a good picture with only a title that meets the challenge description?  This is the kind of thing that is discouraging people from entering a challenge, and causing them to leave this site and go to others.  Sorry, but this pic should not even be in the top 100.<br/> <br/>PS - (bubeltruble), I would like to know how you knew this was Irene M''s picture, and did it affect your vote.  I noticed it was during the challenge, and was not added in after because it was not edited.  Is this some new way of cheating?  I don''t understand how anyone could possibly know how this is one particular persons picture when there are thousands of members on this site.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2009-05-06 18:20:52.</i></td>', 'Congrats Irene.   This is a wonderful picture.  No doubt if you would have used a green liquid, this would have definitely been a top 10.  However, this goes to show that you cannot do well in a challenge even if the picture is within challenge description.  The title of this picture is the only thing I see that has anything to do with green.  Other than that, this picture does not even meet the challenge description.  This picture should have been voted on by challenge description, not title.  This should have not done better than 50 percintile in this challenge, as it does not meet the challenge.  When are the voters going to vote on challenge descriptions and the thought that goes into them instead of a good picture with only a title that meets the challenge description?  This is the kind of thing that is discouraging people from entering a challenge, and causing them to leave this site and go to others.  Sorry, but this pic should not even be in the top 100. PS - (bubeltruble), I would like to know how you knew this was Irene M''s picture, and did it affect your vote.  I noticed it was during the challenge, and was not added in after because it was not edited.  Is this some new way of cheating?  I don''t understand how anyone could possibly know how this is one particular persons picture when there are thousands of members on this site.', '2009-05-06 16:43:14.000000', '2009-05-06 19:20:52.000000', 0),
